      ],
      'Grammar can change a claim scope. Students who finished the draft may leave identifies only the students meeting the condition: the relative clause is restrictive. The students, who finished the draft, may leave presents completion as supplementary information about the whole identified group. Commas therefore affect meaning, not merely pauses. Modifiers also need clear attachment: Having reviewed the evidence, Mina revised her claim makes Mina the reviewer. Use parallel constructions for comparable ideas: to observe, to record and to compare. Edited grammar should preserve the intended meaning rather than apply rules mechanically.',
