      'Original passage: The empty bench waited beneath the station clock. Mina touched the folded ticket but did not unfold it. When the train arrived, she stepped back. An analysis might argue that the passage creates hesitation about departure. Waited personifies the bench and prolongs anticipation. The folded ticket and stepping back supply actions supporting reluctance. Summary reports these events; analysis explains how the chosen details work together. The passage does not state why Mina hesitates, so an interpretation should not invent a family tragedy or a missed deadline as fact. More than one reading may be defensible if it explains the evidence.',
