      ],
      'Use this invented source for practice only: Lira, 2024, School Reading Trial, page 3: Twelve of twenty volunteers visited the reading corner twice. A quotation reproduces exact words and needs quotation marks plus attribution. A paraphrase restates the idea in genuinely new wording and structure, while still naming its source. For example, Lira reports that twelve participants made at least two visits during the trial. The evidence concerns volunteers in one trial, not every pupil. This lesson uses a simple author-year-page teaching model; follow the citation style assigned in a real course. The source and figures are invented and must not be cited as real research.',
