      ],
      'An analytical essay explains how a text constructs meaning. Use the original station scene: Mina holds a folded ticket, leaves it folded, and steps back when the train arrives. A focused thesis is The scene builds hesitation through withheld actions and time imagery. One paragraph can analyze the ticket; another can analyze the clock and arrival. Each begins with an analytical point, cites relevant wording, and explains its contribution. A thesis should not simply announce This essay is about Mina. A conclusion can draw together the pattern while respecting what the passage leaves unresolved, such as her exact reason.',
